+    // stands on the open face's plane (a boss on the opened top, a pocket's walls above its
+    // floor) would be cut away up to the margin, so its inner wall would start above the
+    // plane. The open faces then stay on their plane; the cut is clean because they are
+    // coplanar with the body's own faces there, which the Boolean handles.
+    // Only verified for bodies of planes and cylinders: with other faces (tori from fillets,
+    // spheres, cones, free-form) the margin-0 cut can produce intersection curves that the
+    // tessellator recurses on without end (a robustness seed took 66 GB), so those bodies keep
+    // the old path and its refusals.
+    let tol = (healed.size() * 1e-7).max(1e-9) * 100.0;
+    let simple = healed
